  "id": "pr-280",
  "instruction": "glom.cli — Execute glom transformations and specs directly from the console on JSON, YAML, TOML, or Python target data read from arguments, files, or standard input.\n\nRequired behavior: I was using glom in a script this week, specifically to extract single values from API calls. I noticed I kept having to trim the quotes and whitespace off of the JSON output, because even when it's a single value, it's quoted and followed by a newline. So this feature strips the quotes and whitespace when passed a new flag: . This is only done when the glom result is not a collection. If it is, it falls back to normal json output. Some items to consider: 1. Name? 1. Should it be an error if the output is not a single value? 1. Right now, output is always json. Would it be better to do ? None of these are blockers, I am good to merge as is.\n\nImplement the behavior exercised by these repository scenarios:\n\n- cli scalar\n\nPreserve existing behavior outside these scenarios. A different implementation is acceptable when it produces the same observable results and the designated tests plus the broader suite pass.\n\nRelevant files: glom/cli.py.",
